<article class="env-proposition" id="03FZ">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03FZ">Proposition <span data-tag="03FZ">7.6.2.40</span> <span class="named">(Transitivity)</span>.</a> Let $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be a functor of $\infty $-categories and let $\sigma : \Delta ^2 \times \Delta ^1 \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be diagram, which we depict informally as </p>
<div class="equation" id="03G0">
<span class="equation-label"><a data-tag="03G0" href="/tag/03G0">7.75</a></span>
<div>\begin{equation}  \begin{gathered}\label{equation:transitivity-pullback-square} \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ X' \ar [r] \ar [d] &amp;  Y' \ar [r] \ar [d] &amp;  Z' \ar [d] \\ X \ar [r] &amp;  Y \ar [r] &amp;  Z. } \end{gathered} \end{equation}</div>
</div>
<p> Then: </p>
<p><dl>
<dt>$(1)$</dt>
<dd><p>
Assume that the right square of (<a data-tag="03G0" href="/tag/03G0">7.75</a>) is a $U$-pullback. Then the left square is a $U$-pullback diagram if and only if the outer rectangle is a $U$-pullback diagram. 
</p>
</dd>
<dt>$(2)$</dt>
<dd><p>
Assume that the left square of (<a data-tag="03G0" href="/tag/03G0">7.75</a>) is a $U$-pushout. Then the left square is a $U$-pushout diagram if and only if the outer rectangle is a $U$-pushout diagram. 
</p>
</dd>
</dl></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      We will prove $(1)$; the proof of $(2)$ is similar. Let $A$ denote the partially ordered set $([2] \times [1] ) \setminus \{  (0,0) \} $. Note that the inclusion maps 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  A \setminus \{  (2,0), (2,1) \}  \hookrightarrow A \quad \quad A \setminus \{  (1,0), (1,1) \}  \hookrightarrow A \setminus \{  (1,0) \}  \]
</div>
<p>
       admit right adjoints, and therefore induce left cofinal morphisms 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( A \setminus \{  (2,0), (2,1) \}  ) \hookrightarrow \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }(A) \quad \quad \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( A \setminus \{  (1,0), (1,1) \} ) \hookrightarrow \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }(A \setminus \{  (1,0) \} ) \]
</div>
<p>
       (Corollary <a data-tag="02P3" href="/tag/02P3">7.2.3.7</a>). Applying Corollary <a data-tag="02XQ" href="/tag/02XQ">7.2.2.2</a>, we obtain the following: 
    <p>
<ul>
<li><p>
The left square of (<a data-tag="03G0" href="/tag/03G0">7.75</a>) is a $U$-pullback diagram if and only if $\sigma $ is a $U$-limit diagram. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The outer rectangle of (<a data-tag="03G0" href="/tag/03G0">7.75</a>) is a $U$-pullback diagram if and only if the restriction $\sigma |_{ \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( ([2] \times [1] ) \setminus \{  (1,0) \}  )}$ is a $U$-limit diagram. 
</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>
       If the right square of (<a data-tag="03G0" href="/tag/03G0">7.75</a>) is a $U$-pullback diagram, then $\sigma |_{\operatorname{N}_{\bullet }(A)}$ is $U$-right Kan extended from $\sigma |_{ \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( A \setminus \{  (1,0) \}  )}$, so the desired equivalence follows from Proposition <a data-tag="030V" href="/tag/030V">7.3.8.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</p></p></p></p></p></p></article>
